  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5421",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to KYSE-140, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704 and P2X purinoceptor 1, both of which are subsequently targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is the common target of all three entities, reinforcing its role as a central mediator in the pathway. The final link between Mollicellin N and KYSE-140 is through this intermediate compound, which suggests a potential mechanism involving the activation of P2X receptors or the modulation of signaling pathways through A704. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a key player in the interaction between Mollicellin N and KYSE-140, with the exact nature of the molecular interaction remaining to be elucidated.",
